# angeliqueheduin.fr — partial redesign rules

Source of truth: @docs/CAHIER-DES-CHARGES.md — read it before touching any file.

## Context
Static showcase website of a painter.
Work: text content, shop already removed, fixing broken features, security,
and simplifying the home page (hero / portrait / parcours / atelier / démarche)
so it does not look like a generated template.

**Design freeze (updated):** do not change layout, colors or visual structure of
`#gallery-section` or `#contact-section` (including the Leaflet map). Palette and
type on the rest of the home page stay the same (cream, terracotta, Cormorant / DM Sans).
Do not edit gallery or contact CSS/JS unless asked.

## Project structure — read before editing anything
- `oeuvres/*.html` — these pages EXIST in this project. Do not assume they are missing;
  check locally first. Some of them may be generated (see next point) rather than
  hand-written: check before editing.
- `tools/build_pages.py`, `tools/check_site.py`, `tools/render_test.py` — build/check
  scripts. Before editing any file under `oeuvres/` (or any file you suspect is
  generated), check whether `build_pages.py` produces it from a template or data
  source. If it does, edit the source/template, never the generated output — an
  edit to a generated file is lost on the next build. Say explicitly which case
  applies before editing.
- `AGENTS.md` at the project root may contain instructions read by other agents/tools
  besides Cursor. Read it once at the start of the project and flag any conflict or
  duplication with `.cursor/rules/`. Do not silently let the two diverge.

## Task order (never all at once)
1. Remove the shop (`boutique.html`, `boutique.css`, `boutique.js`) and every reference to it. Replace the "Acquérir l'œuvre" cart flow with a scroll/link to the contact form (subject "Acquisition d'une œuvre", artwork name appended to the message body).
2. Fix the contact form (the Formspree ID stays a clearly marked placeholder) and add a honeypot.
3. Rewrite text, ONE block at a time, waiting for approval between blocks.
4. Technical and security checks (CSP, social links, artwork detail pages).

## Validation gates
- Before starting: read the docs and confirm the scope in a few lines.
- After task 1: list every modified/deleted file and every removed link.
- Text: propose one block, wait for validation, then the next.
- Never decide alone: replacement of the percentage skill bars, testimonials, which social links are real, `oeuvres/*.html` pages that may not exist. Propose or flag, then wait.
- When a real piece of information is missing, say so explicitly. Never guess.

## Design freeze
Do not change layout, colors or visual structure of the collection (`#gallery-section`)
or the contact block (`#contact-section`, map included). Do not edit their CSS/JS unless asked.
The rest of the home page may be simplified (less template chrome) while keeping the same palette and type.
Removing markup/CSS/JS that only served the shop or the cart remains in scope.

## Language
- Replies to the user: French.
- Code identifiers and comments: keep the language already used in the existing code. If unclear, ask.
